lisa-design:
- API pin: github.com/compliance-framework/api v0.19.1-0.20260930152307-aa005f7646ab (approved PR #465 head aa005f7). That branch is based on api b52a187 and does NOT contain api main's #464 (types.PolicyArtifacts, sdk.Artifact*, which agent main's runner/policy_artifacts.go already uses since api v0.20.0-rc2), and it conflicts with api main (sdk/client.go etc.). So `go build ./...` on this pin fails in runner/ until the API PR merges main and the agent re-pins. All local build/vet/test ran through an out-of-repo go.work pointing at a local merge of aa005f7 + api main (181097e) with only sdk/client.go conflicts resolved (keep both AgentConfig and Artifact). Conservative choice: honour the requested pin rather than invent a fork/replace; recorded as an open question.
- Declared vs runtime (R4): agentconfig.Config decoded by viper's weak decoder (R51); toRuntime builds the private structs; agentConfigurationHash stays on the runtime form (golden test recorded before the refactor in its own commit).
- R34 tolerated set T is exactly /plugins/<p>/schedule. Everything else file-origin is fatal, including agentconfig's env-location (${env:} outside plugins.*.config, e.g. in policy_data/labels) and negative verbosity — both follow the shared Validate (code wins) and the LLD's "new-feature rules are not in T".
- Divergence from LLD names: ResolveEnv's sentinel is agentconfig.ErrEnvMissing (LLD said ErrEnvUnset); PolicyBundleExtendsReport is an alias of PolicyExtendsReport; WillApply returns mode-report/mode-off reasons, but prepare never reaches WillApply outside apply modes (overlay is dropped first).
- regocheck.ValidatePolicyBundles runs ONCE per bundle in prepare (step 8.1); inlinepolicy.Check does only parity compile + transitive denied-builtin walk + tests (LLD listed static checks inside Check too; running both would duplicate errors).
- Swap decision uses candidate.identity = sha256(CanonicalJSON(declared incl. api block and secrets) + inline dirs), in memory only; the reported digest (which omits api and masks secrets) is not enough to detect e.g. an api.url or secret change. sameAsActive compares the base raw bytes + fingerprint and the overlay ETag/revision so polls do not re-prepare (and re-run OPA checks) every tick.
- The reconciler owns its own sdk.Client for the config routes (built from the locked file api block, rebuilt when it changes); AgentRunner keeps its own for heartbeat/evidence. Costs one extra token request; avoids sharing mutable runner state across goroutines.
- Reload drain (R33): cron plugin jobs run with context.WithoutCancel(runCtx) so a swap does not cut API calls of in-flight runs; runDaemon waits up to reloadDrainTimeout (5m) then kills plugin clients. SIGTERM keeps 30s + os.Exit(0).
- Protocol cache stores only annotation-derived versions (a successful fetch without the annotation is not cached, same as before).
- --instance-id/CCF_INSTANCE_ID that is not a UUID fails startup (silently ignoring it would register a different instance).
- A run failure after a swap is handed to the reconciler goroutine over a channel (onRunFailed): report failed/internal, failed backoff for that overlay, and cache.Applied reverts to the running candidate's overlay.
- Report truncation step 3 ("drop base") sends base as {} (the wire field is not omitempty). cache-corrupt is reported once: cleared after the first successful report.
- Inline materialization needs a writable state dir (failed/internal otherwise). If a vendor tree has both root data.yaml/yml and data.json and `data` is set, they are merged yaml-then-json-then-data into data.json.
- Evidence prop agent-config-revision is only added when AppliedRevision > 0 (revision 0 = empty overlay / file only). Namespace constant CCFPropNamespace is defined in the agent (the SDK exports none).
- Not implemented (deferred): the end-to-end test with a fake v2 plugin binary receiving the materialized dir in Init/Eval; evidence-v3 BundleIndex provenance (conditional on evidence-v3 G1, not on main).
